items.details:
Expected: finalRelease is refused unless all of the following hold:
- every track is completed;
- no open point is open or in-progress, including points the supplier answered that Beiersdorf has not yet decided;
- completenessBlockers(c) is empty;
- the actor is an active supplier contact of the case's supplier.
The release dialog lists the blockers with jump links. Under BRM v2 the supplier edits directly until the release, so the final app has no correction-request screen before the release. After the release, any change attempt is refused and logged, and a later change means a new case (src/features/supplier/PhaseViews.tsx:240). Test, unit: each blocker type alone makes finalRelease return the state unchanged with a toast; an internal user and a deactivated contact are refused. Test, E2E: the release button shows the blocker list.

Expected: finalRelease creates c.finalDocument exactly once (id, generatedAt, content hash, frozen content snapshot) with no user action. Content:
- CIQ ID, material, supplier (DUNS), template and rule-set versions;
- the released answers of active sections (visible fields only), the K2.1 table and the justifications;
- the evidence list (file name, upload date, uploader);
- every open point's full thread in order (question, answers, returns, edits, close), with who, when and the section/field/row reference, attachments by file name only, never embedded;
- the confirmations (completeness, each review completion including RMM's, the final release) with name, e-mail and time.
It excludes internal notes, RMES records, findings, decisions and internal reasons. It is shown to RMM and the Auditor on the case and sent to the RMM owner's inbox. Nothing can regenerate or change it: finalRelease again, cancel, reopen and edits are all refused. Test, unit: the builder includes all threads (including withdrawn ones) and excludes internal marker strings; the hash is stable; a second finalRelease and any later write leave finalDocument deep-equal. Test, E2E: release, open the document, and find each open-point thread text.

